WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:07.870
Just hours before flying off to Palm Beach,
Florida, and skipping the inauguration, Donald

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.970
Trump issued his final list of pardons and
he is not on the list and his children are

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:14.970
not on the list.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.940
And we will talk a little bit about why momentarily.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.250
A lot of speculation about that.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:26.929
But the list does include a variety of individuals,
143 pardons, maybe most prominently.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:33.160
Steve Benen, former White House chief strategist
and close adviser to Donald Trump, pardoned.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.180
Now, the INS saying there is nothing more
Trump than the following.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:44.940
Steve Bannon was arrested for felony fraud,
for defrauding build the wall donors.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.780
These were pro Trump donors who wanted to
build the wall.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.100
They donated to this, hey, give us money and
we'll build it.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:01:00.070
And it was a total scam. Trump pardoned the
guy who scammed Trump's own supporters.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:04.890
And if you needed any more proof that Trump
never cared about his supporters beyond how

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.150
they were useful to him politically, it is
the pardon of Steve Bannon.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.870
How many times does Trump need to betray his
own supporters before they realized Trump

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.390
never cared about them to begin with?

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:23.410
Also pardoned Eliot Broider, former Republican
finance chair Kwame Kilpatrick, former Democratic

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.010
mayor of Detroit.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.190
Randy Duke Cunningham, a former Republican
congressman.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:33.060
Rick Renzi, former Republican Congressman
Robin Hayes, former Republican congressman

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.750
to rappers Lil Wayne and Chodak Black.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.700
Notably missing from the list are pardons
for his family and pardons for himself.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.060
And this apparently was the culmination of
a pretty dramatic couple of days where on

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.320
Saturday evening, this is a report from CNN.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.320
Donald Trump was warned he had a long meeting
with his advisers on Saturday night.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:03.650
And at that point, he still was leaning towards
pardoning in advance his children, his son

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.700
in law, maybe Rudy Giuliani and possibly even
himself.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.170
And he was told, don't do it.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:16.720
He was told if you pardon them and even yourself,
you will be placing yourself in a legally

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.569
perilous position.

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:21.500
It will convey the appearance of guilt.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.760
It will potentially make you more vulnerable
to reprisals.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:34.340
And indeed, Donald Trump acquiesced to that
and decided not to pardon his children and

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.010
not to pardon himself.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:41.690
Some of these warnings came from White House
counsel Patrick Polony, as well as another

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.450
attorney, Eric Hirschmann, who was involved
in defending Trump in his first impeachment

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.450
trial.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.330
And they all said to Trump, do not pardon
yourself, do not pardon your family.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:58.420
Do not pardon any anybody in a prospective
manner unless you will list specific crimes.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.459
And that was the concern.

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:01.660
A blanket preemptive pardon.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:08.390
Had Trump said, well, I pardon Ivanka in advance
for campaign finance crimes.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:11.640
As an example, this lawyer said that would
be better.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.210
But it also is pointing a finger at specific
crimes you believe maybe they would be charged

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.210
with.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.489
And in the end, Trump deciding I'm not going
to pardon any of them.

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:26.879
And even after Saturday, Trump kept bringing
this up, even after people around Trump thought

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.220
it's done, he's not going to pardon his kids
or himself.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.820
Trump kept bringing it up, bringing it up,
bringing it up.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.230
And the final meeting reportedly where Trump
finally was convinced, OK, I'm not going to

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.520
do it, took place on a Saturday evening.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:47.560
And it's interesting as a general thing, because
Trump has often ignored advice given advice

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.810
given to him.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.730
In fact, Trump ignoring advice given to him
as responsible for much of the trouble that

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.150
he got into during his presidency.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:01.459
And there is a reason why defense attorneys
say, even if you think you had nothing to

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:05.240
do with the crime, it's better not to answer
questions to law enforcement.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.380
Just call a lawyer and say, you don't want
to say anything.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.760
There's a reason why that's the case.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.440
And much of Donald Trump's trouble.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.720
If we look back at his beleaguered four years,
much of that trouble caused by.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.489
From choosing to speak rather than not by
Trump, Trump choosing to act rather than doing

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.729
nothing and just waiting for things to happen
without his involvement, and I don't know

00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:26.090
if there is a lesson here.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:33.800
I mean, the real lesson should be how on earth
how how can we prevent 75 million people from

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.979
being bamboozled by this guy and thinking
it's a good idea to elect him?

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:41.120
That's really the lesson that hopefully we
would learn and and somehow prevent in the

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.120
future.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.120
I don't know if that's the case.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.499
I don't know if that has been learned.

00:04:44.499 --> 00:04:47.569
But the pardon list, the final pardon list
is out.

00:04:47.569 --> 00:04:54.240
So this is the end of the Trump era and the
beginning of the Biden era.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.099
Tomorrow, we will have the timing of today
made it difficult to have inauguration coverage

00:04:58.099 --> 00:04:59.449
today on the show.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:00.819
We'll be covering it live.

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:02.190
And maybe you're with us right now.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.949
Maybe you watched it earlier with us.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:07.089
Tomorrow, we will have coverage of the Biden
inaugural.

00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:11.729
The initial speech scheduled to have a press
briefing already from trumpeting Biden's incoming

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:14.400
press secretary, Jen Psaki, tonight.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.110
And then Joe Biden already scheduled today
to sign a bunch of executive orders, which

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:24.110
you can be sure we will be looking at tomorrow
and seeing if Joe Biden sticks to his promises.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.119
So quick break.

00:05:26.119 --> 00:05:28.259
Let me know your thoughts about what's good.

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:33.060
Excuse me, what's going on on Twitter, where
you can find me at David Pakman.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:44.169
And then a bunch of final stories to tie up
some 

00:05:44.169 --> 00:07:00.879
loose ends coming up here, The David Pakman
